ype":"answer_delta","text":"1] [FRU-RAD-"}},{"dt":34,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":"02] [TM"}},{"dt":33,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":"-M09-GPU].\n**Public precedent"}},{"dt":40,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":"**\nA news report describes the Dec."}},{"dt":27,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":" 2022 Soyuz MS-22"}},{"dt":35,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":" radiator coolant leak attributed to a micrometeor"}},{"dt":33,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":"oid strike and imaged by Canadarm2"}},{"dt":34,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":" as a small hole [WEB-1"}},{"dt":33,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":"]. An agency blog says Russia launched un"}},{"dt":35,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":"crewed Soyuz MS-23 as"}},{"dt":34,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":" a replacement crew"}},{"dt":34,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":"-return vehicle rather than repairing"}},{"dt":33,"event":{"type":"answer_delta","text":" on-orbit [WEB-2].\n"}},{"dt":166,"event":{"type":"usage","usage":{"label":"answer","role":"answer","model":"muse-spark-1.3","effort":"high","ms":46396,"promptTokens":5594,"completionTokens":6847,"reasoningTokens":6184,"costUsd":0.03609225}}},{"dt":0,"event":{"type":"thinking","label":"answer","model":"muse-spark-1.3","effort":"high","text":"Synthesizing telemetry and module records while reconciling conflicting temperature trend values and citing sources.\nQuantifying single-loop thermal margin and validating repair feasibility against pressure, reach, and proximity constraints."}},{"dt":3,"event":{"type":"answer","markdown":"**Diagnosis**\nLoop B leaked and FDIR closed its isolation valve, leaving loop A to carry the full 7.4 kW at 92 % util which exceeds single-loop rejection of 6.1 kW at 85 °C GPU [TR-1180] [BLD-M09]. TM-M09-GPU reads 64.3 °C at t=500 s (+2.3 °C residual, +0.25 °C/min) projecting 85 °C throttle at t=2043 s in 1543 s, with FE-0924 warning projecting 85 °C throttle at t≈2040 s [TM-M09-GPU]. Single-loop limit is ≤74 % util (saturates at about 76 % util) [TR-1180], so without action M-09 throttles then hits 95 °C shutdown [TM-M09-GPU]. Radiator B is field-replaceable (4 latches, 12 N·m, 22 min, 2 panels carried) with no NCR against it [FRU-RAD-02]; NCR-0356 and NCR-0371 are closed on radiator A and J14 [NCR-0356] [NCR-0371].\n**What the cameras show**\nCAM-2 at 4 m shows black star-burst hole with scorch marks venting white particle plume about a panel-width outward at top edge just right of striped radiator latch [CAM-2]. Grapple fixture on +X face centre is clear and PDU panel not visible [CAM-2]. SAM 3.1 on CAM-3 targeted SEG-1 on the grapple fixture at 0.03 m, 1.65 m from the puncture ≥0.5 m and 1.66 m from shoulder ≤2.6 m [CAM-3] [SEG-1] [TR-0640] [FRU-RAD-02].\n**Decision**\nMIGRATE_WORKLOADS M-09 to M-04, M-03, M-05, auto: deadline t=1918 s before AOS t=4500 s, drains 92 % to 70 % ≤74 % in 122 s [TR-1180] [TM-M09-GPU].\nREPAIR_FRU radiator_b with grasp SEG-1, auto: deadline t=1918 s before AOS t=4500 s, 1.65 m keepout and corridor-v ≤0.17 m/s [SEG-1] [FRU-RAD-02] [TM-M09-GPU].\n**Public precedent**\nA news report describes the Dec. 2022 Soyuz MS-22 radiator coolant leak attributed to a micrometeoroid strike and imaged by Canadarm2 as a small hole [WEB-1]. An agency blog says Russia launched uncrewed Soyuz MS-23 as a replacement crew-return vehicle rather than repairing on-orbit [WEB-2].","citations":[{"type":"record","id":"TR-1180","label":"M-09 thermal-vacuum test: single-loop rejection"},{"type":"record","id":"BLD-M09","label":"M-09 build traveler"},{"type":"telemetry","id":"TM-M09-GPU","label":"TM-M09-GPU (FDIR channel)"},{"type":"event","id":"FE-0924","label":"GPU trend +0.95 °C/min on one loop at 92 % util; projects 85 °C throttle at t≈2040"},{"type":"record","id":"FRU-RAD-02","label":"Radiator panel: field-replaceable unit"},{"type":"record","id":"NCR-0356","label":"Radiator A coating scratch (closed)"},{"type":"record","id":"NCR-0371","label":"Connector J14 torque out of spec (closed)"},{"type":"camera","id":"CAM-2","label":"Damage site close-up, 4 m"},{"type":"camera","id":"CAM-3","label":"Grapple fixture + latch B, 4 m"},{"type":"segment","id":"SEG-1","label":"grapple fixture (matched as \"circle\") in CAM-3"},{"type":"record","id":"TR-0640","label":"Servicer arm reach and grapple qualification"},{"type":"web","id":"WEB-1","label":"gizmodo.com","url":"https://gizmodo.com/roscosmos-and-nasa-have-a-plan-to-replace-damaged-soyuz-1849936172"},{"type":"web","id":"WEB-2","label":"nasa.gov","url":"https://www.nasa.gov/blogs/spacestation/2023/01/11/nasa-roscosmos-provide-soyuz-status-provide-crew-flight-schedule-update/"}],"unknownIds":[],"numbers":{"checked":27,"unsupported":[]}}},{"dt":0,"event":{"type":"done","totals":{"promptTokens":48737,"completionTokens":15226,"costUsd":0.13303765,"toolCalls":7,"ms":103239}}}]